                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 65,
                "retweet_count": 18,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Healthcare is so unaffordable that even as a member of Congress I do not take the House plan, and millions of families are stuck in the same broken system. It\u2019s no coincidence that healthcare premiums skyrocketed after Obamacare was implemented.\n\nDemocrats kept the government closed for 43 days over subsidies that touch a small slice of the market while 1.5 million workers went without pay and nothing about a doctor\u2019s visit got cheaper. \n\nNow that the government is open again, our job is to spend the next year driving down costs for working families instead of pretending band-aids are a real fix.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1763055436,
                "view_count": 3411
